<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Salamis</h1><p class="st-meta">1100 BCE – 306 BCE (approx.) · capital Salamis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The leading city-kingdom of ancient Cyprus, whose king Evagoras I united much of the island and defied the Persian Empire for a decade.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Salamis was founded on the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> in the 11th century BCE, succeeding nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enkomi">Enkomi</a> as its harbour silted up. Greek tradition named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teucer">Teucer</a>, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajax-the-great">Ajax</a>, as its founder. Its royal tombs of the 8th and 7th centuries BCE, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a> and sacrificed horses, recall Homeric burial customs.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kings of Salamis were often the most powerful on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evelthon">Evelthon</a> struck some of the island's earliest coins in the 6th century BCE, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onesilus">Onesilus</a> led the Cypriot revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in 498 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evagoras-i">Evagoras I</a>, who reigned from 411 to 374 BCE, promoted Greek culture, allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> and fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> until a negotiated peace in 380 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicocreon">Nicocreon</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I</a> and died c. 310 BCE, and in 306 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-i-of-macedon">Demetrius Poliorcetes</a> won a great naval battle off Salamis. The kingdom then passed under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a>. Salamis remained a major city, renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salamis-cyprus">Constantia</a>, until abandoned after the Arab raids of the 7th century CE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1100 BCE – 306 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:37.81%;width:15.80%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1100 BCE – 306 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Salamis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Evelthon, Evagoras I, Nicocreon</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arcado-Cypriot Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cyprus">Cyprus</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cypriot Salamis</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-703&amp;focus=kingdom-of-salamis" aria-label="Kingdom of Salamis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5539 906 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Salamis lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5859 1162L6092 1134M5859 1162L6140 1251M5859 1162L5772 1297"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6092 1134h0M6140 1251h0M5772 1297h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5859 1162h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5859 1162h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Salamis. <a href="/atlas?year=-703&amp;focus=kingdom-of-salamis">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

